PART 1: WHAT THIS TOOL IS FOR
1.1 Purpose – Read This First
You are designing zone boundaries for a water network. You must decide which pipes should connect zones and which should separate them.
This tool allows you to:
•	DESIGN different zone connection configurations
•	OPTIMIZE which pipes remain open based on your priorities
•	TEST your designs by running hydraulic simulations
•	SEE THE IMPACT immediately through visualization
Think of this as a design workspace where you can experiment with configurations, evaluate the results, refine your approach, and save the solutions that perform best.
________________________________________
1.2 What You Are Actually Doing
You are not simply analyzing an existing system. You are actively designing how zones connect.
You control:
•	Which pipes serve as open connections between zones
•	Which pipes are closed to create separation
•	How many connections each zone pair should have
•	Whether to keep the largest, smallest, shortest, or highest-flow pipes
•	How the hydraulic behavior changes when you modify the design
Every change is a design decision, and the system immediately shows you the hydraulic consequences.
