PART 5: DESIGNING MANUALLY
5.1 Interactive Mode
When Interactive Mode is enabled:
•	Hover over pipes to identify them.
•	Click a green pipe to close it.
•	Click a red pipe to open it.
•	Dark blue pipes are not boundaries and cannot be toggled.
The dashboard updates immediately as you modify the design.
________________________________________
5.2 Manual Design Strategies
Start from All Open
•	Click “Open all.”
•	Close selected pipes manually.
Start from All Closed
•	Click “Close all.”
•	Open selected pipes manually.
Hide Closed Boundaries
•	Enable “Hide closed boundaries.”
•	Only open pipes remain visible.
________________________________________
PART 6: TESTING YOUR DESIGNS
6.1 Running a Simulation
Click ⚡ Simulate to test your current configuration.
The system calculates:
•	Flow in every pipe
•	Pressure at every node
•	Velocity and headloss
Results are based entirely on your open/closed design.
Run a simulation:
•	After major design changes
•	Before saving
•	When comparing alternatives
If the simulation fails, adjust the configuration. The network may be hydraulically disconnected or overly restricted.
________________________________________
6.2 Visual Testing Tools
Animation (▶️ Animate)
Shows:
•	Flow direction
•	Active flow paths
•	Which pipes carry flow
Flow Values (💧 Show Values)
Displays exact numerical flow values on open pipes.
Data Table (📋 Table)
Allows:
•	Sorting by any attribute
•	Identifying extreme values
•	Clicking rows to highlight elements
•	Exporting results
Colormap (🎨 Colormap)
Colors nodes by attribute values, helping you quickly identify pressure or demand patterns.
________________________________________
6.3 What to Evaluate
•	Are pressures acceptable across all zones?
•	Are flows balanced?
•	Are any pipes overloaded?
•	Is redundancy sufficient?
•	Are any zones under-supplied?
________________________________________
PART 7: OPTIMIZING YOUR DESIGN
Optimization means improving the design to meet specific goals.
Goal	Strategy
Minimize cost	Fewer, smaller open pipes
Maximize redundancy	More, larger connections
Improve pressure	Increase connections
Create isolation	Reduce connections to zero
Balance flow	Adjust prioritization rules
Use an iterative process:
1.	Design
2.	Simulate
3.	Evaluate
4.	Adjust
5.	Repeat
Continue until performance meets your objectives.
